00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:15.150 align:start position:0%
the spine consists of a series of  interconnected bones call  extending from the base of the skull to  the tailbone each vertebra connects with  a one above and below at the facet  joints allowing them to move relative to  one another in between each bony  vertebra lies a shock absorbing  intervertebral discs the facet joints  and intervertebral discs work together  to permit the bending and twisting  motions of the back and neck protected  within the vertebral column is the  spinal cord which connects the brain to  the rest of the body spinal nerves  emanate from the spinal cord at regular  intervals
 

